From 5d9dcf2c46ca9b5a6640916d161278b64c575fb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:56:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 05/18] fix(shadow): attach and look up shadow roots in the
 caller's own document

op_shadow_attach and op_shadow_root_info always used the page's document,
while every other DOM call names its realm's frame. Inside a frame realm,
body.attachShadow() therefore created the shadow root in the page's tree,
keyed by the frame's node id, and the first appendChild into it (in the
frame's tree) failed with HierarchyRequestError.

Cloudflare Turnstile does exactly this in its challenge frame (it attaches a
shadow root to its <body> and appends a <style>), so every Cloudflare-fronted
page such as stackoverflow.com threw that error from the challenge.

Both ops now take the realm frame id, as op_dom does.

